From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:17:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(delegation): reuse read-only focused failure snapshots
 [daveey]

Focused subagent.list polls opened the async ledger writer on every call.
Even after schema-once reconciliation, writer setup applied durability
barriers and cloned configuration plus chmod on every read. A real-store
209-call cProfile replay attributed 1.306s cumulative wall to that setup.
Existing failure-surface tests checked output, not writer/bootstrap work.

Use bounded thread-local read-only handles and commit-keyed scoped SQL
snapshots. Evaluate the 24h cutoff each call, retaining its inclusive
boundary and clock rollback behavior. Never memoize RPC authorization,
live children, progress or process observations. Errors discard handles;
missing/schema-unready stores are not created or migrated by polling.

RED: no-writer and missing-store tests failed on base; no-rescan due-time
test failed on uncached read-only intermediate. GREEN: targeted consumers
and focused tests; complete consumer suite follows on this commit.
Real-dispatch fixture replay (2 owners, 2000 foreign rows, 209 calls,
21 unrelated commits, one relevant update): before 0.368490 CPU seconds,
after 0.030386 seconds (1.763111 vs 0.145389 ms/call). Fixture evidence is
not live whole-rpc acceptance; parent J retains the <=1% core gate.
